"""
TACTILE LOCAL-GLOBAL SYNCHRONISED WITH THE ECG (test version)
-------------------------------------------------------------
- 4 tactile blocks (monotone/discordant x left/right), random order.
- Fixation cross only (no visual task).
- 25 habituation + 120-130 test trials per block, 20% Global Deviants.
- Electrical stimulator ON/OFF (start-up dialog):
    * ON : full trigger (bits 64/128 drive the stimulators, pins 8/9).
    * OFF: same trigger WITHOUT bits 64/128 -> the EEG gets the marker, no stimulation.
- Real-time ECG via RDA (BrainVision Recorder, 32-bit port 51244).

ECG ALGORITHM
- Online R-peak detection (5-30 Hz band-pass + adaptive threshold + refinement on the raw signal).
- Predicted R = last R + mean of the last 8 valid RR intervals (300-2000 ms).
- Beat 1 at predicted R - 270 ms. SOA 150 ms -> beat 4 at R+180, beat 5 at R+330.
  Beats 2 and 3 are not sent (as in the original script).
- ITI: beat 1 can only be sent if >= ITI_req has elapsed since the previous beat 5,
  with ITI_req drawn at random from 1350-1650 ms. Otherwise, wait for the next R.

RDA LATENCY
- Sample times are anchored to the PC clock using the arrival of the RDA blocks.
- If the triggers come back through RDA as markers, they are used to correct the
  remaining latency (automatic correction, printed to the console).

BEFORE STARTING ON THE PLATFORM
- In Recorder: enable Remote Data Access (Configuration > Preferences) and be in monitoring/recording.
- Enter the IP of the Recorder computer and the exact ECG channel name in the dialog.
- "Simulation" mode: synthetic ECG from a local RDA server, to test without the platform.
"""

